es2 =  oxed{200}. so the qualitative inspection covers:  oxed{200	ext{ predictions}} under this reading of the deck's sampling description. this is a derived calculation; the slide states the per-task/per-language counts rather than explicitly writing “200.” 5.35.4 failure mode 1 — hallucination the first major failure is:  oxed{	ext{hallucination}} the deck says that in cross-lingual summarization, the model regularly invents details that are absent from the source article . (source: indicgenbench-slides) this is particularly serious for summarization. 5.35.5 what should a summary do? suppose source document d contains facts: f(d)=\{f_1,f_2,\ldots,f_n\}. a faithful summary should primarily compress information already supported by d :  oxed{ s\approx 	ext{compressed representation of }d } it should not introduce an unsupported: f_{n+1}
